    "id": "L1",
    "type": "mc",
    "text": "Find $lim[x->-1] frac{sqrt(x + 2) - 1}{x + 1}$. Plugging in gives $frac{0}{0}$, and there is a square root. Multiply top and bottom by the **conjugate** of the top, which is",
    "options": [
     "$sqrt(x + 2) + 1$",
     "$sqrt(x + 2) - 1$",
     "$x + 1$",
     "$sqrt(x + 2)$"
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "hint": "Flip the sign in the middle.",
    "explain": "$(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2$ gets rid of the root."
   },
